# The example prompts of the web app's sidebar and demo mode (issue #27).
# Each names a prompt family with a deterministic rule or seed-backed answer in
# the engine, mirroring the multilingual and hello-world end-to-end tests, so a
# regression in the seed surfaces when a user clicks the prompt. Kept as data,
# not code, so no answer is keyed to one of these prompts (R1188-U1).
example-prompts
  example "Greeting (en)" "Hi"
  example "Greeting (ru)" "Привет"
  example "Greeting (hi)" "नमस्ते"
  example "Greeting (zh)" "你好"
  example "Farewell (en)" "Goodbye"
  example "Farewell (ru)" "До свидания"
  example "Farewell (hi)" "अलविदा"
  example "Farewell (zh)" "再见"
  example "Identity (en)" "Who are you?"
  example "Identity (ru)" "Кто ты?"
  example "Identity (hi)" "तुम कौन हो?"
  example "Identity (zh)" "你是谁?"
  example "Clarification (en)" "I don't understand"
  example "Clarification (ru)" "не понял"
  example "Clarification (hi)" "समझ नहीं आया"
  example "Clarification (zh)" "我不明白"
  example "Capabilities (en)" "What can you do?"
  example "Capabilities (ru)" "Что ты умеешь?"
  example "Behavior rules" "List behavior rules"
  example "Self facts" "List all facts you know about yourself"
  example "Hello world (Rust)" "Write me hello world program in Rust"
  example "Hello world (Python)" "Create a hello world example in Python"
  example "Hello world (JavaScript)" "Write hello world in JavaScript"
  example "Hello world (TypeScript)" "Write hello world in TypeScript"
  example "Hello world (Go)" "Show hello world in Go"
  example "Hello world (C)" "Show hello world in C"
  example "Calculation (en)" "What is 2 + 2?"
  example "Calculation (ru)" "Сколько будет два плюс два?"
  example "Concept (en)" "What is Rust?"
